        "original_id": "c41eebfa-dbd5-5047-9601-9984fd17480a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Reginald Engelbach\n- Places: Cairo, Harageh, Egypt\n- Organizations: Egyptian Museum of Cairo\n- Roles: Egyptologist, engineer\n- Topics: archaeology, museum artifact registers\n\nFacts:\n- Reginald Engelbach was born on July 9, 1888, and he was an English Egyptologist and engineer.\n- In 1913, Reginald Engelbach excavated the cemeteries at Harageh.\n- Reginald Engelbach is mainly known for his work at the Egyptian Museum of Cairo, especially for compiling a register of the museum's artifacts.\n- Cairo is the capital and largest city of Egypt.\n- Reginald Engelbach died on February 26, 1946.",
